David Arthur created KAFKA-15435:
------------------------------------

             Summary: KRaft migration record counts in log message are inco=
rrect
                 Key: KAFKA-15435
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15435
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: kraft
    Affects Versions: 3.6.0
            Reporter: David Arthur


The counting logic in MigrationManifest is incorrect and produces invalid o=
utput. This information is critical for users wanting to validate the resul=
t of a migration.

=C2=A0
{code}
Completed migration of metadata from ZooKeeper to KRaft. 7117 records were =
generated in 54253 ms across 1629 batches. The record types were {TOPIC_REC=
ORD=3D2, CONFIG_RECORD=3D2, PARTITION_RECORD=3D2, ACCESS_CONTROL_ENTRY_RECO=
RD=3D2, PRODUCER_IDS_RECORD=3D1}.=20
{code}

Due to the logic bug, the counts will never exceed 2.



