Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Jos=C3=A9 Armando Garc=C3=ADa Sancio created KAFKA-15509:
--------------------------------------------------

             Summary: KRaft Controller doesn't consider brokers that are sh=
utting down during topic creating
                 Key: KAFKA-15509
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15509
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Jos=C3=A9 Armando Garc=C3=ADa Sancio
            Assignee: Jos=C3=A9 Armando Garc=C3=ADa Sancio


The topic creation implementation in KRaft is able to user brokers that are=
 fenced as replicas during topic creations. The restriction is that the con=
troller won't assign leadership to those topics.

This feature makes it possible for users to roll clusters with 3 brokers wi=
thout sacrificing topic creation availability.

Looking at the code it looks like the KRaft controller doesn't consider bro=
kers that are shutting down as eligible for replicas during topic creation.



--
