migruiz4 created KAFKA-15513:
--------------------------------

             Summary: KRaft cluster fails with SCRAM authentication enabled=
 for control-plane
                 Key: KAFKA-15513
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15513
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: migruiz4


We have observed a scenario where a KRaft cluster fails to bootstrap when u=
sing SCRAM authentication for controller-to-controller communications.

The steps to reproduce are simple:
 * Deploy (at least) 2 Kafka servers using latest version 3.5.1.
 * Configure a KRaft cluster, where the controller listener uses SASL_PLAIN=
TEXT + SCRAM-SHA-256 or SCRAM-SHA-512. In my case, I'm using the recommende=
d in-line jaas config '{{{}listener.name.<controller-name>.scram-sha-512.sa=
sl.jaas.config{}}}'
 * Run 'kafka-storage.sh' in both nodes using option '--add-scram' to creat=
e the SCRAM user.

When initialized, Controllers will fail to connect to each other with an au=
thentication error:

=C2=A0
{code:java}
[2023-08-01 11:12:45,295] ERROR [kafka-1-raft-outbound-request-thread]: Fai=
led to send the following request due to authentication error: ClientReques=
t(expectResponse=3Dtrue, callback=3Dkafka.raft.KafkaNetworkChannel$$Lambda$=
687/0x00007f27d443fc60@2aba6075, destination=3D0, correlationId=3D129, clie=
ntId=3Draft-client-1, createdTimeMs=3D1690888364960, requestBuilder=3DVoteR=
equestData(clusterId=3D'abcdefghijklmnopqrstug', topics=3D[TopicData(topicN=
ame=3D'__cluster_metadata', partitions=3D[PartitionData(partitionIndex=3D0,=
 candidateEpoch=3D4, candidateId=3D1, lastOffsetEpoch=3D0, lastOffset=3D0)]=
)])) (kafka.raft.RaftSendThread) {code}
Some additional details about the scenario that we tested out:
 * =C2=A0Controller listener does work when configured with SASL+PLAIN
 * The issue only affects the Controller listener, SCRAM users created usin=
g the same method work for data-plane listeners and inter-broker listeners.

=C2=A0

Below you can find the exact configuration and command used to deploy:
 * server.properties

{code:java}
listeners=3DINTERNAL://:9092,CLIENT://:9091,CONTROLLER://:9093
advertised.listeners=3DINTERNAL://kafka-0:9092,CLIENT://:9091
listener.security.protocol.map=3DINTERNAL:PLAINTEXT,CLIENT:PLAINTEXT,CONTRO=
LLER:SASL_PLAINTEXT
num.network.threads=3D3
num.io.threads=3D8
socket.send.buffer.bytes=3D102400
socket.receive.buffer.bytes=3D102400
socket.request.max.bytes=3D104857600
log.dirs=3D/bitnami/kafka/data
num.partitions=3D1
num.recovery.threads.per.data.dir=3D1
offsets.topic.replication.factor=3D1
transaction.state.log.replication.factor=3D1
transaction.state.log.min.isr=3D1
log.retention.hours=3D168
log.retention.check.interval.ms=3D300000
controller.listener.names=3DCONTROLLER
controller.quorum.voters=3D0@kafka-0:9093,1@kafka-1:9093
inter.broker.listener.name=3DINTERNAL
node.id=3D0
process.roles=3Dcontroller,broker
sasl.enabled.mechanisms=3DPLAIN,SCRAM-SHA-256,SCRAM-SHA-512
sasl.mechanism.controller.protocol=3DSCRAM-SHA-512
listener.name.controller.sasl.enabled.mechanisms=3DSCRAM-SHA-512
listener.name.controller.scram-sha-512.sasl.jaas.config=3Dorg.apache.kafka.=
common.security.scram.ScramLoginModule required username=3D"controller_user=
" password=3D"controller_password";{code}

 * kafka-storage.sh command

{code:java}
kafka-storage.sh format --config /path/to/server.properties --ignore-format=
ted --cluster-id abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv --add-scram SCRAM-SHA-512=3D[name=
=3Dcontroller_user,password=3Dcontroller_password] {code}



