When a client application depends on the kafka-client library the jlink too=
l can not be used to generate a custom JDK because the client jar is treate=
d as an automatic module.=C2=A0

The module-info class can be generated for the JAR files using the jdeps to=
ol or a module-info can be created by hand for each jar. I believe the curr=
ent structure of the Kafka code can be used as is.

